- op: discuss  # 72af
  at: '2026-09-09T21:33:43Z'  # 72af
  by: agent  # 72af
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 72af
  clock: 4  # 72af
  nonce: 72af  # 72af
  message: "FIXED AND MEASURED 2026-09-09, same day as filing. PR on branch\njgstern-agent/fix/scala-receiver-type-module-slot, commit c9d2aad2fd.\nRecord: docs/measurements/0024-scala-receiver-type-module-slot.md; instrument\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sigog_scala_slot_09092026/ (PLAN.md pre-registered\nbefore any A-arm number existed, ADJUDICATION.txt the per-row census).\n\nTHE FIX is one expression: the module segment now carries\nimport_aliases.get(receiver_type) when the file itself declares a path for that\ntype, plus the matching ExternalRef. call_construct=\"method\",\nreceiver_type_hint, evidence_type=\"ast_call\" and confidence 0.40 are all\nunchanged and pinned by tests -- the first because it is the phantom-barrier\nguard, the last two because re-pricing 40,970 edges inside a recall fix would\nmake the A/B unattributable (filed separately).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, two independent repositories, the item's own filed repro\nre-run on both arms:\n\n    repo   scala external method-call edges typed\n    sbt      0 / 10,985  (0.00%)  ->  595 / 11,032  (5.39%)\n    lila     0 / 29,985  (0.00%)  ->  317 / 30,019  (1.06%)\n\n    method-kind catalogue rows reached VIA SCALA's OWN edges (was 0/164)\n    sbt      0 -> 13     io-boundary chains via scala edges   0 -> 38\n    lila     1 ->  2                                          1 ->  2\n\nThe 14 gained rows are 14/14 CORRECT on a CENSUS read-back against source --\nevery one a real Java I/O method on a receiver whose declared type matches the\nslot, with the import present in the same file. Zero false positives. Ten\nproduction-path tests pin the fix, including three controls (project-class\nreceiver, untyped receiver, unimported type) that passed BEFORE the change and\nso cannot have been fixed into passing.\n\nTHE DIRECTION HAZARD THIS ITEM NAMED DID NOT MATERIALISE, and it was measured\nrather than assumed. sanitized_flows is 0 -> 0 on every repo and no claim\nverdict moved. What DID move at L4 is the closed-world disclosure: untypable\nreceivers 11,177/11,645 (95.98%) -> 10,629/11,692 (90.91%) on sbt and\n40,157/40,739 (98.57%) -> 39,874/40,773 (97.80%) on lila, with the host_fs\nuntyped-call caveat dropping 450 -> 416 sites and database 103 -> 90. 548 sbt\nand 283 lila call sites became examinable and NONE became a violation.\n\nCONTROLS: killbill (java, 0 .scala files -- the load-bearing one, since scala's\ncatalogue MERGES java's) and modsecurity (cpp) produce BYTE-IDENTICAL\nverify-claims JSON across the arms, under a comparison that includes the caveat\ndigest.\n\nTWO PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTIONS WERE REFUTED, both toward MORE effect: sbt typed\nshare 5.39% against a predicted 1-4%, and sbt chains 38 against a predicted\n1-15. I discounted too hard for Scala's implicit imports and project types; a\nbuild tool imports java.io types explicitly far more than a web application\ndoes. The error is in the flattering direction, which is the one to distrust.\n\nWHAT THIS CLOSURE DOES **NOT** CLAIM. The item's exposure figure (90% of\nscala's 184 rows at risk via R1) is NOT discharged. Measured before predicting,\nonly 10.1% (sbt) / 4.8% (lila) of these edges carry receiver_type_hint AT ALL,\nso this fix reached 53% and 22% of its own achievable ceiling and the remaining\n~90-95% carry no inferred type for any downstream change to route. That is a\ndistinct, larger defect filed as WI-pokam (var_types coverage), with one cheap\nconfirmed mechanism -- `val b: java.io.File = ...` yields no hint, because a\nqualified type is not a type_identifier node -- and one hard one needing the\nreturn-type registry objc/swift already have. Also filed: WI-vafot (wildcard\nimports contribute no hint and the fallback mis-registers the package's last\nsegment; Scala's implicit imports unmodelled) and WI-sabam (this branch\nhand-rolls Edge.create instead of make_unresolved_edge).\n\nClosing on the FILED ROW -- the slot is the defect this item names, it is fixed,\nand the catalogue is reachable through scala for the first time on behavioural\nevidence. The residual is filed, not absorbed."  # 72af
